PIXEL WHARF #08
The typeface that ate our budget

We licensed a display face for the rebrand, then spent four weeks finding out
what "per domain" means in a foundry contract. Here is the invoice, annotated.

- What a webfont licence actually counts (hint: not visitors).
- Three foundries whose terms fit on one screen.
- The open face we would have shipped instead, in hindsight.

Studio notes at the bottom, as always.

